                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "056bb28f-1032-37b8-a74a-0cb6bb0ba90b",
                        "entry_id": "c32e7f1c-5a25-3bd7-8896-d20b823271e7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nose."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72ff4299-4dac-4ac2-a6d2-ab8dd713ca8b",
                                "sense_id": "056bb28f-1032-37b8-a74a-0cb6bb0ba90b",
                                "text": "[…] you have got J-E-W written right across the middle of that face—look at the shnoz on him, for God’s sakes!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae8e23d0-6d8d-48df-b12c-d89622ec3739",
                                "sense_id": "056bb28f-1032-37b8-a74a-0cb6bb0ba90b",
                                "text": "There's a TV commercial out now for a nasal spray in which a man in need of a decongestant wakes up to find that his entire head has turned into a giant schnozz."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "daea8212-d328-4c85-83ed-b481cd594267",
                                "sense_id": "056bb28f-1032-37b8-a74a-0cb6bb0ba90b",
                                "text": "One presumes the anesthetic is for the bull, although if I were about to pound a nail through some bull's schnozz I might want some anesthetic myself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3aa5f473-32b7-4e48-9c2f-d19e2e1e7f6b",
                                "sense_id": "056bb28f-1032-37b8-a74a-0cb6bb0ba90b",
                                "text": "In another talk, a DinoNose collaborator, Scott Sampson of the University of Utah, Salt Lake City, pointed out a number of ridges in the ceratopsian schnozz that probably supported curtains of cartilage; these in turn may have served as scaffolding for layers upon layers of mucous membranes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
